Tuesday Update
Trade Alert: AG calls exited for loss; buy CRM callsStocks swing higher as =
investors hunt for bargains and anticipate stimulus packageStocks are rippi=
ng higher again while Treasuries declined ahead of key technology earnings =
and as investors weighed progress in pandemic stimulus talks.Through midday=
, the Dow advanced by 576.74, or 1.9%, with the S&amp;P 500 higher by 1.7% =
to 3,838.53 and the Nasdaq Composite Index up by 1.7% to 13,627.81. Communi=
cation services, energy, and financials were among the biggest gainers, wit=
h all sectors in the green.The US 10-year yield rose by 2.4 basis points to=
 1.1%. West Texas Intermediate crude oil futures climbed 2.3% to $54.77.Ind=
ex heavyweights Amazon (AMZN) and Alphabet (GOOG) are set to report quarter=
ly results after the market close. Alphabet likely will benefit from an acc=
eleration in search advertising, according to BofA Securities, which recent=
ly said Amazon will probably report higher-than-expected results due to COV=
ID-19 driven e-commerce market share gains over the holiday period in Q4.Pr=
esident Joe Biden reportedly met with a group of 10 Republican senators Mon=
day to muster support for a bipartisan stimulus program, seeking to bridge =
the gap between his $1.9 trillion proposal and about $600 billion that curr=
ently seems to be forthcoming from across the aisle, according to media rep=
orts. But, if the deal doesn't come through, House Speaker Nancy Pelosi and=
 Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer are said to be prepared to push the $=
1,400 stimulus checks and other aid along partisan lines."It's critical we =
have money to do vaccinations and testing," Dallas Federal Reserve Presiden=
t Robert Kaplan was cited as saying on CNBC Tuesday. "It's critical that pe=
ople who are out of work have continued relief beyond March."Upside support=
 tanked in the stocks that were recently posting outsized gains from the Re=
ddit-fueled short squeeze. Stocks posting declines included GameStop (GME),=
 which fell 49%; AMC Entertainment (AMC) slumped 39%; and BlackBerry (BB) w=
as off 20% intraday.Portfolio: We exited AG calls for a big 71% loss today =
unfortunately. That will happen occasionally and is why we always recommend=
 using less than 20% of capital on any single trade. =E2=80=A6 CAT calls or=
der did not fill. ... We have one new idea for you. *CURRENT RECOMMENDATION=
First Majestic Silver (AG) February $17 calls-- Symbol: AG210219C00017000--=
 Bought at $6.10 on Monday-- Sold at $1.60 on stop today for a 73% loss*NEW=
 RECOMMENDATIONSalesforce (CRM) February 235 calls-- Symbol: CRM210219C0023=
5000-- Order: Buy at $5.50 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to sell half at=
 $7.15 lmt gtc and half at $9.35 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at $3.85 stp=
, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only&nbsp;*Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are=
 for monthly options expiring on the third Friday of the specified month un=
less otherwise noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unle=
ss otherwise specified. All orders are good for the day only unless otherwi=
se noted. "Day only" orders expire at the close of the current session. Pas=
t results are no guarantee of future returns. All accounts may not achieve =
comparable results. Recommendations are leveraged and speculative, so only =
use risk capital =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. All results =
are shown ex-commissions and fees. Options trading involves the risk of sub=
stantial loss. Some news and research provided by Wall Street Journal, Bloo=
mberg, Associated Press, MT Newswires and Reuters.&nbsp;

